{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2334","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2334","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2334\",\"parent_revision\":\"7476a87f116f821efecf087f38c872d69c603b0db400ce399d3b38002e0d14d1\",\"root_revision\":\"7476a87f116f821efecf087f38c872d69c603b0db400ce399d3b38002e0d14d1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe summarizer quality gate stop hook fires on every sub-agent session including non-summarizer agents (e.g. dh:code-reviewer). The hook's STEP 1 correctly no-ops for non-summarizer agent types by outputting {} immediately, but the hook infrastructure still invokes it and surfaces the reasoning trace as stop hook feedback noise in every session.\\n\\nThe fix is to add an agent_type filter at the hook registration level in settings.json so the hook is never invoked for agent types outside the summarizer set (file-summarizer, url-summarizer, image-summarizer). This eliminates the repeated feedback messages without changing hook logic.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **add agent_type filter to summarizer stop hook registration** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed during dh:code-reviewer session \u2014 hook fired 5 times with no-op output\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-21)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n4/10 \u2014 Noise reduction only; no functional breakage. The hook correctly no-ops for non-summarizer agents (STEP 1 guard in validate-summarizer-output.cjs). The fix eliminates unnecessary hook invocations and reduces reasoning trace noise in sessions that use non-summarizer agents heavily (e.g., dh:code-reviewer).\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Nothing blocked; this is pure noise reduction.\\n- Bottleneck: Every non-summarizer SubagentStop event invokes `validate-summarizer-output.cjs`, which reads the transcript and outputs `{}`. The hook infrastructure still records the invocation, and the reasoning trace appears as feedback noise in every session using sub-agents (e.g., dh:code-reviewer, task-worker).\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nThe `validate-summarizer-output.cjs` hook is invoked only when a SubagentStop event carries an `agent_type` matching `^(file-summarizer|url-summarizer|image-summarizer)$`. Non-summarizer agent stops (e.g., `dh:code-reviewer`, `task-worker`, `general-purpose`) produce no hook invocation and no feedback noise.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nObservable end state:\\n- `plugins/summarizer/hooks/hooks.json` SubagentStop entry already has `\\\"matcher\\\": \\\"^(file-summarizer|url-summarizer|image-summarizer)$\\\"` \u2014 this is the correct registration point (confirmed present in current source).\\n- Verification: a SubagentStop event with `agent_type: \\\"dh:code-reviewer\\\"` does not invoke `validate-summarizer-output.cjs`.\\n- Note: if the issue manifests despite the existing matcher, the investigation must determine whether the hook is registered via a separate path (e.g., project `settings.json` hooks block or a second hooks.json entry) that lacks the matcher filter.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running a `dh:code-reviewer` sub-agent session produces no `validate-summarizer-output.cjs` invocation in the hook trace.\\n2. Running a `file-summarizer` sub-agent session still invokes `validate-summarizer-output.cjs`.\\n3. `plugins/summarizer/hooks/hooks.json` SubagentStop entry has `matcher: \\\"^(file-summarizer|url-summarizer|image-summarizer)$\\\"`.\\n4. No change to hook logic inside `validate-summarizer-output.cjs` is required \u2014 only registration-level filtering.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/summarizer/hooks/hooks.json (already has correct matcher) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/summarizer/hooks/validate-summarizer-output.cjs |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json (reference for hook registration pattern) |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-guide |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-io-api |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Investigation required: `plugins/summarizer/hooks/hooks.json` already has the correct `matcher` filter on SubagentStop. Before implementing, verify how the hook is being invoked for non-summarizer agents \u2014 the root cause may be a duplicate registration elsewhere (e.g., a second hooks block in `.claude/settings.json` or a separate hook file) rather than a missing matcher in the plugin hooks.json.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 if root cause is a missing matcher, the fix is a single-field edit in hooks.json. Investigation to locate the duplicate registration point is the primary effort. No logic changes required.\\n\",\"digest\":\"ec8b6417b9234102f2597b929804ba1714a1443cd13be5b38db12f304e4384b3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCRS5Q\"}"}